        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Tura Beach, Merimbula, New South Wales, Australia, Bega Valley Shire, Spokane, Washington\n- People: Elwood Curtin Zimmerman\n- Roles: American entomologist\n- Products: Insects of Hawaii, Australian Weevils (Coleoptera: Curculionoidea)\n- Organizations: University of Hawaiʻi Press, CSIRO\n- Topics: population, local government area\n\nFacts:\n- Elwood Curtin Zimmerman was born in Spokane, Washington, on December 8, 1912.\n- Tura Beach is a suburb of Merimbula on the South Coast of New South Wales, Australia, in the Bega Valley Shire local government area.\n- Elwood Curtin Zimmerman was an American entomologist best known for the multivolume series Insects of Hawaii, published by the University of Hawaiʻi Press, and Australian Weevils (Coleoptera: Curculionoidea), published by CSIRO.\n- The population of Merimbula was 3,544 at the 2016 census.\n- Elwood Curtin Zimmerman died in Tura Beach, New South Wales, on June 18, 2004.",
